{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelope_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelope_value","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeSum.lean#L115-L125","doc":"**On the unit circle, against `dx/dφ = i·x`, that is `2φ`.**\n\n`Σⱼ ∂V/∂x · (i·x) = −2·log x · i`, and with `log(e^{iφ}) = iφ` this is\n`−2·iφ·i = 2φ` — real, which is why `S` is real and its derivative is `2φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sum_dVdx_of_pinned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sum_dVdx_of_pinned","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeSum.lean#L101-L113","doc":"The same, with the logarithms put back. Stated separately so that no tactic\never sees a `log` while clearing denominators — an earlier draft let `field_simp`\nrewrite `1 - y/x` to `(x-y)/x` *inside* the logarithm, which changes the branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sum_div_of_pinned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sum_div_of_pinned","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeSum.lean#L89-L99","doc":"**`Σⱼ ∂V/∂x = −2·log x / x`, given the pinned log-sums.**\n\nPure algebra: the two hypotheses are the branch-pinned values of the log-sums,\nand everything else cancels. The pinning itself is *not* proved here — it needs\n`hcont`, which is open — so it is taken as a hypothesis, which is the honest\nfactoring of analysis from algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_sum_log_one_sub_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_sum_log_one_sub_div","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeSum.lean#L70-L85","doc":"**`exp(Σⱼ log(1 − yⱼ/x)) = x⁻¹`.**\n\n`∏ⱼ(1 − yⱼ/x) = ∏ⱼ(x − yⱼ)/x³ = x²/x³ = 1/x`, using `prod_x_sub` (#4658). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_sum_log_one_sub_x_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_sum_log_one_sub_x_mul","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeSum.lean#L55-L68","doc":"**`exp(Σⱼ log(1 − x·yⱼ)) = x`.**\n\nThe exponential of the first log-sum is `∏ⱼ(1 − x·yⱼ)`, which Vieta makes `x`\n(`prod_one_sub_x_mul`, #4658). No analysis, no branch choice. ","signatureChunk":0}]}